{"seq":2,"slug":"calibration-uncertainty","title":"校准与不确定性：让奖励模型知道自己何时不该自信","url":"/l-doc-books/h/ai-llm/reward-modeling-rlhf/challenges/calibration-uncertainty","wordCount":1726,"readingTime":7,"html":"<h1 id=\"校准与不确定性-让奖励模型知道自己何时不该自信\">校准与不确定性：让奖励模型知道自己何时不该自信</h1><p>奖励黑客最阴险的地方，不在于奖励模型会犯错——任何模型都会犯错——而在于它<strong>犯错时依然一脸笃定</strong>。一个未校准的奖励模型对一条它从没见过的、荒腔走板的回答，可能给出和真正优秀回答一样高的自信分数。当这个过度自信的分数被 RL 拿去当唯一的优化目标，灾难就被放大了。这一篇讲两件互相纠缠的事：奖励模型的分数在概率意义上校准得怎么样、以及怎么让它输出&quot;我对这个打分有多大把握&quot;的不确定性——后者是对抗 <a href=\"reward-hacking\">奖励黑客</a> 与 <a href=\"over-optimization\">过度优化</a> 最有力的抓手之一。</p>\n<h2 id=\"核心概念-校准-vs-分辨-两件不同的事\">核心概念：校准 vs 分辨，两件不同的事</h2><p>先厘清一对常被混淆的概念。<strong>分辨力</strong>（discrimination）是奖励模型能不能把好回答排在坏回答前面——就是 <a href=\"../training/bradley-terry\">Bradley-Terry</a> 里那个成对准确率。<strong>校准</strong>（calibration）则是它给出的概率是否名副其实：当奖励模型说&quot;<span class=\"math-inline\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>w</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">y_w</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.625em;vertical-align:-0.1944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">y</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.1514em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.0359em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.0269em;\">w</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> 有 80% 概率更好&quot;时，在所有它这么说的样本里，是否真的约 80% 确实如此。一个模型完全可能分辨力很强却校准很差（总能排对序，但把 60% 的把握说成 95%），反之亦然。</p>\n<pre class=\"mermaid\" data-diagram-type=\"flowchart\" data-source=\"flowchart TD&#10;    A[奖励模型输出] --&gt; B[分辨力&lt;br/&gt;能否排对序]&#10;    A --&gt; C[校准&lt;br/&gt;概率是否名副其实]&#10;    B --&gt; D[成对准确率高]&#10;    C --&gt; E{预测概率 vs 实际频率}&#10;    E --&gt;|吻合| F[良好校准]&#10;    E --&gt;|概率虚高| G[过度自信&lt;br/&gt;危险]&#10;    E --&gt;|概率虚低| H[欠自信]&#10;    G --&gt; I[RL 里放大分布外错误]&#10;    F --&gt; J[可用不确定性做保守优化]\">flowchart TD\n    A[奖励模型输出] --&gt; B[分辨力&lt;br/&gt;能否排对序]\n    A --&gt; C[校准&lt;br/&gt;概率是否名副其实]\n    B --&gt; D[成对准确率高]\n    C --&gt; E{预测概率 vs 实际频率}\n    E --&gt;|吻合| F[良好校准]\n    E --&gt;|概率虚高| G[过度自信&lt;br/&gt;危险]\n    E --&gt;|概率虚低| H[欠自信]\n    G --&gt; I[RL 里放大分布外错误]\n    F --&gt; J[可用不确定性做保守优化]</pre><p>对奖励建模而言，两者都要，但<strong>校准在接进 RL 后变得格外关键</strong>：RL 会专门去找奖励模型最自信的高分区域猛推，如果那里的自信是虚的，策略就被引向了悬崖。</p>\n<h2 id=\"为什么奖励模型天生难校准\">为什么奖励模型天生难校准</h2><p>奖励建模有一个内建的校准障碍，源于 <a href=\"../foundations/preference-to-reward\">偏好到奖励</a> 里那个&quot;只约束差、不约束绝对尺度&quot;的事实。Bradley-Terry 损失只关心 <span class=\"math-inline\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">r(y_w) - r(y_l)</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0278em;\">r</span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">y</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.1514em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.0359em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.0269em;\">w</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">−</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0278em;\">r</span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">y</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3361em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.0359em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.0197em;\">l</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span></span></span></span></span>，因此训练根本不约束奖励的绝对数值有多大——模型可以把所有差都放大十倍来把损失压得更低，代价是把每个概率都推向 0 或 1，也就是系统性过度自信。这不是训练 bug，而是损失函数的固有倾向。</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>现象</th>\n<th>表现</th>\n<th>后果</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td>尺度膨胀</td>\n<td>奖励差被无节制放大</td>\n<td>概率饱和到 0/1，过度自信</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>分布外自信</td>\n<td>对没见过的回答仍给极端分</td>\n<td>RL 被引向盲区</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>温度失配</td>\n<td>未做温度缩放校准</td>\n<td>概率不可作决策依据</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>最直接的补救是<strong>温度缩放</strong>（temperature scaling）：训练后在验证集上拟合一个标量温度 <span class=\"math-inline\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">T</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1389em;\">T</span></span></span></span></span>，把奖励差除以 <span class=\"math-inline\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">T</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1389em;\">T</span></span></span></span></span> 再过 sigmoid，使输出概率与实际频率对齐。这是分类校准里最简单有效的手段，几乎零成本，却常被奖励建模流程省略。评估校准好坏用可靠性图（reliability diagram）和期望校准误差（ECE）。</p>\n<h2 id=\"用集成估计认知不确定性\">用集成估计认知不确定性</h2><p>温度缩放解决的是&quot;概率是否名副其实&quot;，但还有一个更深的问题：奖励模型能不能对<strong>它自己没把握的输入</strong>说&quot;我不知道&quot;？这需要认知不确定性（epistemic uncertainty）——由数据不足、分布外导致的不确定，理论上可以靠更多数据消除。估计它的主力手段是 <a href=\"../training/reward-architecture\">奖励模型架构</a> 里提过的<strong>集成</strong>：训 <span class=\"math-inline\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">K</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0715em;\">K</span></span></span></span></span> 个奖励模型，对同一回答，它们打分的方差就是认知不确定性的估计。</p>\n<div class=\"math-block\"><span class=\"katex-display\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"block\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mtext>used</mtext></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>r</mi><mo>ˉ</mo></mover><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo>⋅</mo><mtext>std</mtext><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"true\" minsize=\"1.2em\" maxsize=\"1.2em\">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><mo>…</mo><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"true\" minsize=\"1.2em\" maxsize=\"1.2em\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">r_{\\text{used}}(y) = \\bar{r}(y) - \\lambda \\cdot \\text{std}\\big(r_1(y), \\dots, r_K(y)\\big)</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0278em;\">r</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3361em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.0278em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord text mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">used</span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">y</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord accent\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.5678em;\"><span style=\"top:-3em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0278em;\">r</span></span><span style=\"top:-3em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"accent-body\" style=\"left:-0.1944em;\"><span class=\"mord\">ˉ</span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">y</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">−</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">λ</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">⋅</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1.2em;vertical-align:-0.35em;\"></span><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">std</span></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"delimsizing size1\">(</span></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0278em;\">r</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3011em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.0278em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">1</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">y</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"minner\">…</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0278em;\">r</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3283em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.0278em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.0715em;\">K</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">y</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"delimsizing size1\">)</span></span></span></span></span></span></div><p>这个&quot;均值减 <span class=\"math-inline\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\lambda</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">λ</span></span></span></span></span> 倍标准差&quot;的<strong>保守奖励</strong>（也叫下置信界，LCB）是对抗奖励黑客的利器：在几个模型意见一致的区域（低方差），奖励几乎不打折；在它们分歧的区域（高方差，多半是分布外或黑客高发区），奖励被大幅惩罚，RL 就没动力往那里钻。<span class=\"math-inline\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\lambda</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">λ</span></span></span></span></span> 是保守程度的旋钮，太大则策略畏手畏脚学不动，太小则形同虚设。多篇 2026 综述（如 arXiv:2505.02686）把不确定性感知的奖励建模列为过度优化的主要缓解方向。</p>\n<h2 id=\"不确定性的两种来源要分开处理\">不确定性的两种来源要分开处理</h2><p>不是所有不确定性都该被惩罚。要区分两类：<strong>认知不确定性</strong>来自模型知识不足（该惩罚、可通过补数据消除），<strong>偶然不确定性</strong>（aleatoric）来自任务本身的固有分歧——比如一对回答确实见仁见智、人类标注者本就 50/50（这不该被当成&quot;模型没学会&quot;来惩罚，硬压反而抹平真实的价值多元）。集成方差主要捕捉前者；后者更多体现在单个模型对该样本预测概率接近 0.5。实务上，对高偶然不确定性的样本，正确做法是承认&quot;这里没有唯一正确答案&quot;，而非逼奖励模型给出一个虚假的确定判断。这一区分与 <a href=\"../training/preference-data\">偏好数据</a> 里&quot;人类标注者间只有 75% 一致&quot;的观察是同一枚硬币的两面。</p>\n<h2 id=\"校准如何进入实践决策\">校准如何进入实践决策</h2><p>校准和不确定性最终要落到操作上。上线前，用可靠性图检查奖励模型是否过度自信、做温度缩放；训练 RL 时，用集成的保守奖励限制策略往高不确定区跑、并把集成方差当奖励黑客的实时警报；监控时，盯住&quot;策略生成回答上的平均奖励不确定性&quot;是否随训练放大（放大即预警分布外漂移）。这套操作是 <a href=\"../practice/reward-modeling-in-practice\">落地与边界</a> 里质量门的一部分。核心心法：一个诚实的奖励模型，价值不只在于打分准，更在于<strong>知道自己什么时候打不准</strong>。</p>\n<h2 id=\"小结\">小结</h2><ul>\n<li>分辨力（能否排对序）与校准（概率是否名副其实）是两件事，接进 RL 后校准格外关键。</li>\n<li>Bradley-Terry 只约束奖励差、不约束绝对尺度，天生倾向尺度膨胀与过度自信；温度缩放是低成本补救。</li>\n<li>集成方差估计认知不确定性，据此构造&quot;均值减 <span class=\"math-inline\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\lambda</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">λ</span></span></span></span></span> 倍标准差&quot;的保守奖励，能有效遏制奖励黑客与过度优化。</li>\n<li>要区分认知不确定性（该惩罚、可补数据消除）与偶然不确定性（任务固有分歧，不该硬压）。</li>\n<li>实践中校准与不确定性落为：上线前温度缩放 + 可靠性图，RL 中保守奖励 + 方差警报，监控奖励不确定性漂移。</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"延伸阅读\">延伸阅读</h2><ul>\n<li>本 hub：<a href=\"../training/reward-architecture\">奖励模型架构</a> 提供集成这一不确定性来源；<a href=\"reward-hacking\">奖励黑客</a> 是保守奖励要对抗的对象；<a href=\"over-optimization\">过度优化</a> 把不确定性纳入 KL 预算的量化框架。</li>\n<li>跨 hub：<a href=\"../../ai-evaluation-benchmarks/evaluation-fundamentals/metric-types\">28_ai-evaluation-benchmarks / 指标类型</a> 补充校准误差 ECE 等评估指标的通用定义；<a href=\"../../ai-safety-alignment/safety-foundations/safety-evaluation\">13_ai-safety-alignment / 安全评估</a> 讲不确定性在安全评估里的角色。</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"level":1,"text":"校准与不确定性：让奖励模型知道自己何时不该自信","id":"校准与不确定性-让奖励模型知道自己何时不该自信"},{"level":2,"text":"核心概念：校准 vs 分辨，两件不同的事","id":"核心概念-校准-vs-分辨-两件不同的事"},{"level":2,"text":"为什么奖励模型天生难校准","id":"为什么奖励模型天生难校准"},{"level":2,"text":"用集成估计认知不确定性","id":"用集成估计认知不确定性"},{"level":2,"text":"不确定性的两种来源要分开处理","id":"不确定性的两种来源要分开处理"},{"level":2,"text":"校准如何进入实践决策","id":"校准如何进入实践决策"},{"level":2,"text":"小结","id":"小结"},{"level":2,"text":"延伸阅读","id":"延伸阅读"}],"prev":{"title":"奖励黑客：策略学会了骗分而不是变好","url":"/l-doc-books/h/ai-llm/reward-modeling-rlhf/challenges/reward-hacking"},"next":{"title":"过度优化：Goodhart 定律的量化曲线与 KL 缰绳","url":"/l-doc-books/h/ai-llm/reward-modeling-rlhf/challenges/over-optimization"}}